      en: "Lake Malombe is located in southern Malawi and is fed by the Shire River, which flows from Lake Malawi. It is a shallow lake with an average depth of only about 3 meters and a surface area of around 350 km². The lake is rich in fish and supports a significant fishing industry. The surrounding wetlands are important habitats for waterbirds and other wildlife. The lake's water level fluctuates greatly depending on inflows from Lake Malawi. Lake Malombe is ecologically closely linked to the Shire River and is sensitive to changes in the catchment. The region is agricultural, with rice cultivation and fishing as main economic activities.",
