      en: "The Linthipe River is a river in central Malawi, flowing through the town of Salima and emptying into Lake Malawi. It is about 150 kilometers long and an important water source for agriculture in the region. The river is known for its seasonal floods that bring nutrients to surrounding fields. The banks are covered with reeds and grass, providing habitat for waterbirds. The Linthipe River plays a role in local fishing. In the dry season, the river may dry up significantly. Water quality is affected by agricultural runoff and settlements.",
